 "response": "Stedamu's budget is now **$2503K**.\n\n**How I got there:**\n\n1. **Which records count.** Only Finance Office budget updates change the budget. Messages from Engineering, Vendor, PMO, Sales, Legal, Marketing, Operations and Facilities are ignored. Finance Office notices that don't change the amount (audits, reminders, room changes, cost-center codes) are also ignored.\n\n2. **Resolving withdrawals.** Some withdrawals are themselves withdrawn, so I worked back from the latest withdrawal in each chain. Examples:\n   - #0632 withdraws #0439, which revives #0112. #0112 withdraws #0078, which revives #0007. #0007 withdraws #0003, so the \u2212$36K in #0002 still applies.\n   - #1367 withdraws #0845, which revives #0175. #0175 withdraws #0057, which revives #0013. #0013 withdraws #0010, so the \u2212$407K in #0010 does not apply.\n   - #1546 withdraws #1403, which revives #1213. #1213 withdraws #1203, so the +$521K in #1203 does not apply.\n\n   In total, about 100 Finance Office updates end up withdrawn.\n\n3. **Totalling.** The only \"set\" instruction is #0001, at $1880K. I then applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in order. Some checkpoints:\n   - After #0006 (\u2212$562K): $1282K\n   - After #0126: $4482K\n   - After #0448: $895K\n   - After #1111: $3059K\n   - After #1423: $1003K\n   - After the last update, #1598 (+$5K): **$2503K**\n\nANSWER: $2503K",
